{"schema_version":"1.0.0","id":"cik-0001828318","cik":"0001828318","slug":"enovix-828318","name":"Enovix Corp","ticker":"ENVX","exchanges":["Nasdaq"],"sector":"Miscellaneous Electrical Machinery, Equipment & Supplies","sic":"3690","country":"CA","website":"","listed_years":5.4,"first_annual":"2021-03-08","last_filing":"2026-07-28","annual_only":false,"edgar_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001828318&type=10-K","summary":{"sentences":["Enovix Corp files with the SEC under \"Miscellaneous Electrical Machinery, Equipment & Supplies\", based in CA, and has been publicly reporting for 5 years.","It reported $28.2m of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 49.1% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 20.4%.","Listed on Nasdaq, it is still consuming cash, with roughly 57 months of runway at the current burn."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 49.1% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $7.6m in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1828318/000182831826000029/0001828318-26-000029-index.htm","accession":"0001828318-26-000029"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in 7 of the last 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1828318/000182831826000029/0001828318-26-000029-index.htm","accession":"0001828318-26-000029"},{"text":"Gross margin expanded from 5.1% to 20.4% against the same quarter a year earlier - the company is keeping more of what it sells, not buying growth with discounts.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1828318/000182831826000029/0001828318-26-000029-index.htm","accession":"0001828318-26-000029"},{"text":"Net cash of $8.4m against total assets of $833.9m - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1828318/000182831826000029/0001828318-26-000029-index.htm","accession":"0001828318-26-000029"}],"bear":[{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 8124.5% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1828318/000182831826000029/0001828318-26-000029-index.htm","accession":"0001828318-26-000029"},{"text":"Gross margin is only 20.4%, so scale has to be enormous before anything reaches the bottom line.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1828318/000182831826000029/0001828318-26-000029-index.htm","accession":"0001828318-26-000029"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-577.6% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1828318/000182831826000029/0001828318-26-000029-index.htm","accession":"0001828318-26-000029"},{"text":"The operating loss widened by $1.3m against the same quarter a year earlier - it is getting worse, not better.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1828318/000182831826000029/0001828318-26-000029-index.htm","accession":"0001828318-26-000029"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 6.9% over the year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1828318/000182831826000029/0001828318-26-000029-index.htm","accession":"0001828318-26-000029"},{"text":"Debt of $520.4m against equity of $240.7m. Leverage decides who controls the outcome if trading deteriorates, and it is not the shareholder.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1828318/000182831826000029/0001828318-26-000029-index.htm","accession":"0001828318-26-000029"},{"text":"No officer history could be reconstructed from public filings, so the team - the thing that matters most - is the thing we know least about.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001828318"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 12.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.12,"consecutive":2,"current":0.204,"current_display":"20.4%","threshold_display":"12.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 25.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.25,"consecutive":2,"current":0.491,"current_display":"49.1%","threshold_display":"25.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"runway_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Cash runway falls below 12 months","metric":"runway_months","comparison":"below","threshold":12.0,"consecutive":1,"current":57.35,"current_display":"57 months","threshold_display":"12 months","fired":false,"rationale":"Below twelve months the company raises on whatever terms it can get, and that dilution lands on you.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 14.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.14,"consecutive":1,"current":0.069,"current_display":"6.9%","threshold_display":"14.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers y